<title>POLAND: POLISH FOREX RESERVES UP TO $22.86 BLN JULY 1-10.</title>
<headline>POLISH FOREX RESERVES UP TO $22.86 BLN JULY 1-10.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's net foreign currency</p>
<p>reserves grew by $204 million in July 1-10 to $22.857 billion</p>
<p>and were $1.191 billion higher than at the start of the year,</p>
<p>the National Bank of Poland (NBP) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>    POLISH RESERVES (bln dlrs)   JULY 10    JUNE	JULY '96</p>
<p>    Official reserves		 N/A	  N/A	17.797</p>
<p>    Net reserves		     22.857    22.654     21.960</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures in billions of dollars. Official reserves</p>
<p>are those held by the state. Net reserves mean the total amount</p>
<p>of hard currencies in the whole banking system.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
